      "date": "2026-04-07T07:07:36.000Z",
      "title": "METROBRAND: New Sports Format Expansion Will Support Future Returns",
      "body": "Analysts have trimmed their price target on Metro Brands to ₹1,211 from ₹1,272, citing slightly more conservative assumptions for revenue growth, profit margins, the discount rate and future P/E multiples. What's in the News During Third Quarter FY26, Metro Brands opened 35 new stores and closed 11, with 100 openings and 18 closures over the nine-month period, indicating a calibrated approach to expanding its retail network (company disclosure).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/retail/nse-metrobrand/metro-brands-shares/n0ztydha-analysts-lift-metro-brands-price-target-as-profit-margins-improve-and-dividends-announced/updates/19-analysts-have-trimmed-their-price-target-on-metro-brands-to",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
      "id": "b44aaaf1-9bc7-45e3-9955-f098d64588d9",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-01-28T11:35:04.000Z",
      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues exceed analyst expectations",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹4.71 (up from ₹3.48 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹8.27b (up 18% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹1.28b (up 36% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 16% (up from 14% in 3Q 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 3.2%. Earnings per share (EPS) also surpassed analyst estimates by 2.5%. Revenue is forecast to grow 15% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 18% growth forecast for the Specialty Retail industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 2% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 10% per year, which means it is tracking significantly ahead of earnings growth.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "137640c1-ae64-42d5-8737-283e12885b3e",
      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-01-22T10:04:48.000Z",
      "title": "METROBRAND: New Athletic Format Expansion Will Drive Future Returns",
      "body": "Analysts have trimmed their fair value estimate for Metro Brands from ₹1,286.95 to ₹1,272.10 as small tweaks to the discount rate, revenue growth, profit margin assumptions and future P/E expectations flow through their models. What's in the News Board meeting scheduled on January 27, 2026 to consider and approve the unaudited standalone and consolidated financial results for the quarter and nine months ended December 31, 2025, along with the statutory auditors' limited review report (Key Developments).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/retail/nse-metrobrand/metro-brands-shares/n0ztydha-analysts-lift-metro-brands-price-target-as-profit-margins-improve-and-dividends-announced/updates/18-analysts-have-trimmed-their-fair-value-estimate-for-metro-br",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
